vel by an Asian writer, either written in English or translated into English, and published in the previous calendar year.\\n\\nFor many years, as part of The Times Literature ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... His award-winning novels have been adapted for the cinema, shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, and translated into more than thirty languages. His essays and short stories have appeared in The New York Times, The Washington Post, and The New Yorker, among many other publications. Hamid now ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.aspeninstitute.org/blog-posts/20-new-works-fiction-social-impact/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\" ... She is the author of three novels, Frog Moon (1994), translated into French as Kaki (1997), The Jasmine Man (2001), and her most recent novel, The Other Sister (2008). She is also the author of several poetry collections and works of literary criticism, and has translated the works ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d35\"},\"ref\":\"d35\",\"snippet\":\" ... prize more than once), Praiseworthy wins the UK's James Tait Black Prize and is shortlisted for the Dublin Literary Award and the Climate Fiction Prize, among others. Marosia Castaldi's The Hunger of Women wins the ALTA Prize for Prose (for the best translation from any language ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d11\"},\"ref\":\"d11\",\"snippet\":\" ... A selection of his poetry is collected in Desire Never … Read More\\n\\nColm Toíbín\\n\\nColm Toíbín is the author of six novels, including The Master, winner of the International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award and shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, as well as winner of the LA Times ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... Galatta-Banaglore Literature Festival Book Prize for Best Fiction 2017), and The Odd Book of Baby Names. His works have been translated into French, German, and several Indian languages.\\n\\nAshutosh Bhardwaj\\n\\nAuthor\\n\\nAshutosh Bhardwaj is a bilingual journalist, fiction writer and literary critic. He experiments with prose in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.hhousebooks.com/authors/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her work has been translated into over thirty languages. She lives in Gainesville, Florida.\\n\\nMira Jacob\\n\\nMira Jacob is a novelist, memoirist, illustrator, and cultural critic. Her graphic memoir Good Talk: A Memoir in Conversations was shortlisted for the National Book Critics Circle Award, longlisted for the PEN ... \",\"title\":\"https://authorsguild.org/about/team/council-bios/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... His novels have been widely reviewed and translated into a dozen languages. He teaches at Columbia University.\\n\\nRachel Eliza Griffiths\\n\\nOctober 9, 2024\\n\\nRachel Eliza Griffiths is a multi-media artist, poet, and novelist. Her collection of poetry and photography, Seeing the Body (W.W. Norton 2020), was ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsandsciences.syracuse.edu/english-department/creative-writing-mf-program/raymond-carver-reading-series/previous-raymond-carver-reading-series/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"72baca5096ac1207c1e4cb8654158fd2697c8f6445814072ac48e2909fa8f115\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"2e4759a3ae4f4c5decc838026e7da85a250fe84f9b6c2dfda7ecf46bb6cd2df5\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"novel translated into 26 languages shortlisted Man Asian Literary Prize\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d58\"},\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... It has been translated into 50 languages. The most for any author, dead or alive.\\n\\nIn 2005, Time magazine named the \\\"milestone in African literature\\\", Achebe's magnum opus, one of the 'best 100 English language novels written since 1923' — the year Time was founded.\\n\\nThings Fall Apart ... \",\"title\":\"https://paanluelwel.com/2011/10/21/prof-taban-lo-liyong-south-sudanese-literary-icon-and-an-african-philosopher/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d59\"},\"ref\":\"d59\",\"snippet\":\" ... Books of 1998\\\" (year-end best-of) | |\\n| Dec2009 | Planisphere | \\\"Editors' Choice\\\" (recent books of interest) | |\\n| Jun2011 | Illuminations | \\\"Editors' Choice\\\" (recent books of interest) | |\\n\\nOxford-Weidenfeld Translation Prize\\n\\nThe annual Oxford-Weidenfeld Translation Prize is an award recognizing \\\"book-length literary translations into English from any living European language ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_awards_and_honors_received_by_John_Ashbery\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\" ... Scotiabank Giller Prize short list nominee in 2005, winner of the city of Toronto Book Award in 2000 and the recipient of the CBC Canadian Literary Award for short fiction in 2001. Her books have been published in 18 countries and translated into 14 languages and she was ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d60\"},\"ref\":\"d60\",\"snippet\":\" ... The essays in this book explore the many facets of language rights and language protection from a variety of theoretical, legal, and academic perspectives.\\n\\nThe Song of Everlasting Sorrow: A Novel of Shanghai by Wang Anyi, translated by Michael Berry and Susan Chan Egan\\n\\nSet in post-World ... \",\"title\":\"https://translationstudies.complit.ucsb.edu/publications\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d61\"},\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... Selected Prose, 1971-2001 (2002) earned the Truman Capote Award for Literary Criticism, the largest annual prize for literary criticism in the English language. John Carey in the London Sunday Times proposed that Heaney's \\\"is not just another book of literary criticism…It is a record of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poets/seamus-heaney\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\"